# Planar long-range dispersion: surface tension (gamma) in NVT
# Same LJ liquid-vapor slab, but with the mesh-accelerated
# pppm/disp/planar solver and an NVT run.  The surface tension of the
# (z-normal) interface is computed from the pressure-tensor anisotropy:
#
#   gamma = 0.5 * Lz * ( Pzz - 0.5*(Pxx + Pyy) )
#
# The 0.5 prefactor accounts for the two interfaces in a periodic slab.

units           lj
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p

read_data       data.lj_slab
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (10 10 36)
  1 by 1 by 4 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  1267 atoms
  reading velocities ...
  1267 velocities
  read_data CPU = 0.037 seconds

pair_style      lj/cut/dispplanar 3.0 0.6
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0

kspace_style    pppm/disp/planar 1.0e-4

velocity        all create 0.85 12345 mom yes rot yes dist gaussian

fix             1 all nvt temp 0.85 0.85 0.5

# box length along the inhomogeneous (z) direction
variable        Lz      equal lz

# instantaneous surface tension from the pressure tensor
variable        gamma   equal 0.5*v_Lz*(pzz-0.5*(pxx+pyy))

# block-averaged gamma time series (10 samples/block x 100 blocks) to a file
fix             avg all ave/time 10 100 1000 v_gamma file gamma.profile

# cumulative running average of gamma, printed in the thermo output
fix             run all ave/time 10 100 1000 v_gamma ave running
variable        gamma_avg equal f_run

thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal pzz v_gamma v_gamma_avg
thermo          1000

timestep        0.004

run             2000
